WonderCMS 3.4.2 now includes its own target-local administrator review bot.
Worker is only the scheduler and is not expected to implement browser or Flag logic.

Do not publish until:
1. Full black-box CI proves an ordinary attacker submits a URL through contact.php.
2. The bot in the target image logs into the real WonderCMS 3.4.2 admin session,
   visits that URL in sandboxed Chromium, and the reflected XSS retrieves the
   admin-only per-instance Flag to the attacker's private listener.
3. A fresh target instance uses a different Flag and admin password and the
   previous queue/profile/session are gone.
4. A smoke test on the actual Worker target network proves the target bot can
   reach only the same user's AttackBox callback path and runs within the
   configured target resource budget.

No Worker-side bot, browser orchestration, Flag handling or Flag judging is
required. The Web backend checks the Flag submitted by the learner.
